{
  "intro": {
    "title": "42 & The Piscine",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is 42?",
        "text": "École 42 is a tuition-free programming school built on peer-to-peer learning. No teachers, no lectures — you learn by doing projects, reviewing peers, and surviving the Piscine."
      },
      {
        "heading": "The Piscine",
        "text": "A 26-day intensive bootcamp. Shell scripting, C fundamentals, algorithms, exams every week. You sleep at school. You code until it compiles. The moulinette is your judge."
      },
      {
        "heading": "42 Practices",
        "text": "Norminette for style. Git for version control. No forbidden functions. Exact output or zero. Peer evaluation. Exam mode: no internet, no help, just you and vim."
      },
      {
        "heading": "First → Right → Better",
        "text": "Ship the MVP. Fix correctness. Then optimize. This world follows the same loop: walk in, get a ready workspace, code, test with mini, iterate."
      }
    ]
  },
